  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Saskop. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Saskop (also known as Lambapea) is an Estonian trick-taking card game for four players. It is the Estonian member of the prestigious Schafkopf group of games. It distinguishes itself with a 36-card deck (removing 5s and lower) and a complex ranking system where the 6s and Kings occupy the highest tiers of the trump suit. It is a partnership game that emphasizes card counting and aggressive bidding to secure the 61-point victory threshold.',
    objective: 'Score at least 61 points (out of 120 card points) to win the round.',
    gameplay: 'Four players in two partnerships bid 5 to 9 for the right to choose trump. The 6 of the chosen trump suit is highest; then all Kings, Queens, and Jacks in suit order (clubs, spades, hearts, diamonds), then trump suit A-10-9-8-7. Left of dealer leads; must follow suit and must beat the current trick if able. First team to 16 strokes wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Follow suit; picture cards (J, Q, K) count as trumps.',
      'Must trump if void in led suit; must beat highest card in trick if able.',
      '61+ card points wins the round; 16 strokes win the game.',
      'Tie at 60: redeal same trumps, no bidding. All pass: diamonds, winners score 1 stroke.',
    ],
